NAME
     crond - run commands on a schedule

SYNOPSIS
     crond [-n]

DESCRIPTION
     crond wakes every minute and runs whatever /etc/crontab, the files
     in /etc/cron.d and the users' crontabs say to run then. Output goes
     to the log.

OPTIONS
     -n   stay in the foreground

SEE ALSO
     crontab(1), service(8), syslogd(8)
